<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maimonides</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maimonides was a Jewish philosopher, legal scholar and physician born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Cordoba</a> in the twelfth century. His family left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> conquest imposed pressure on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and Christians, and he eventually settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. His works, including the Guide for the Perplexed, made him one of the most influential thinkers of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maimonides.jpg" alt="Maimonides" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blaisio Ugolino · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Moses_Maimonides_in_Thesaurus_antiquitatum_sacrarum.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
